{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_Eynk5lOirjdSubon73FOsjBo","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Complete the openspec CLI commands implementation. IMPORTANT: Your branch is behind master. You MUST first update your branch from master to avoid reverting already-merged changes.\\n\\n**Steps to take:**\\n1. First, merge master into your branch: `git fetch origin && git merge origin/master`\\n2. Resolve any merge conflicts\\n3. Then implement the missing openspec commands\\n\\n**What to implement:**\\n1. `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (creates openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/)\\n2. `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n\\n**Files to read:**\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (for startup protocol references)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see existing command patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes:**\\n- Add commands in tools/se3_tools/commands/openspec.py\\n- Register in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns from other commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- Run `se3 lint` to ensure specs are valid\\n- Run any tests you create\\n\\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT delete or modify files from other tasks (human_calls.py, archive_calls.py, collab.py changes, etc.). These were already merged to master and must be preserved.\\n\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 2, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:53:42.324701\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2508184, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n     2→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2e7779a-53d4-4906-88b6-be418048d4e2","uuid":"7d693f34-ef3d-4974-bd2e-642ab6a5b716","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.collab/tasks/task-001.json","content":"{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Complete the openspec CLI commands implementation. IMPORTANT: Your branch is behind master. You MUST first update your branch from master to avoid reverting already-merged changes.\\n\\n**Steps to take:**\\n1. First, merge master into your branch: `git fetch origin && git merge origin/master`\\n2. Resolve any merge conflicts\\n3. Then implement the missing openspec commands\\n\\n**What to implement:**\\n1. `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (creates openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/)\\n2. `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n\\n**Files to read:**\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (for startup protocol references)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see existing command patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes:**\\n- Add commands in tools/se3_tools/commands/openspec.py\\n- Register in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns from other commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- Run `se3 lint` to ensure specs are valid\\n- Run any tests you create\\n\\n**CRITICAL:** Do NOT delete or modify files from other tasks (human_calls.py, archive_calls.py, collab.py changes, etc.). These were already merged to master and must be preserved.\\n\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 2, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:53:42.324701\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2508184, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n","numLines":2,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_QV7Ydr5psvnEy3b2oRsuVYTA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\"id\": \"task-005\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-input-methods\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-input-methods\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Implement file-based human input method\", \"prompt\": \"Implement support for human input via prompt files as an alternative to MCP calls.\\n\\n**Background**: issues.md mentions: \\\"human\\u4ece\\u4ea4\\u4e92\\u754c\\u9762\\u4e4b\\u5916\\u7684\\u8f93\\u5165\\u65b9\\u5f0f\\uff0c\\u4ee5\\u53ca\\u8f93\\u5165\\u7684\\u5f52\\u6863\\\" (human input methods outside the interaction interface, and archiving of such input). This refers to supporting file-based human input in addition to sync/async MCP calls.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-inputs/` directory structure for file-based human input\\n2. Add `se3 human input --file <path>` command that:\\n   - Reads a prompt file written by the human\\n   - Makes the content available to the agent\\n   - Archives the processed input file\\n3. Add `se3 human input --list` to show pending input files\\n4. Define the input file format (similar to human-calls but reversed - human writes request, agent responds)\\n\\n**File format for human inputs**:\\n```markdown\\n# Human Input: {title}\\n\\n## Context\\n{context provided by human}\\n\\n## Request\\n{what the human wants the agent to do}\\n\\n## Response\\n{agent fills this in}\\n```\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand existing human call patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing patterns)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/ (see command structure)\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- This complements (not replaces) the existing human-as-mcp system\\n- Input files should be archived after processing (to human-inputs/archive/)\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI commands\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**CRITICAL - Merge Conflict Resolution**:\\nYour branch has merge conflicts with master that you MUST resolve before completing:\\n\\n1. **tools/se3_tools/__init__.py** - Version comment conflict:\\n   - Master has: `SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION = \\\"2.5.0\\\"  # Add openspec init/list and human-calls archiving commands`\\n   - Your branch has: `SE3_FRAMEWORK_VERSION = \\\"2.5.0\\\"  # Add se3 human-input command for file-based human input`\\n   - RESOLUTION: Keep version \\\"2.5.0\\\" and combine the comment: `# Add openspec init/list, human-calls archiving, and human-input commands`\\n\\n2. **tools/se3_tools/cli.py** - Import conflict:\\n   - Master imports: `human_calls_cmd`\\n   - Your branch imports: `human_input`\\n   - RESOLUTION: Import BOTH modules:\\n     ```python\\n     from .commands import lint, status, sync, verify, update, collab, commit, openspec, human_calls_cmd, human_input\\n     ```\\n   - Also register BOTH typers:\\n     ```python\\n     app.add_typer(human_calls_cmd.app, name=\\\"human-calls\\\", help=\\\"Manage human calls\\\")\\n     app.add_typer(human_input.app, name=\\\"human\\\", help=\\\"Manage human input\\\")\\n     ```\\n\\n3. **Temporary .prompt files** - Delete all tmp*.prompt files (they are temp files that should not exist)\\n\\n**Steps to resolve**:\\n1. First, check out the conflicting files from master as a base: `git checkout master -- tools/se3_tools/__init__.py tools/se3_tools/cli.py`\\n2. Then manually apply your changes on top, ensuring you keep both human_calls_cmd and human_input\\n3. Delete all tmp*.prompt files\\n4. Complete your implementation\\n5. Run tests with `se3 lint` and any other test commands\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec - this is an additional input method.\\n\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [\"task-003\"], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 2, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:49:47.811271\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2501